From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] blueline: Wi-Fi stage 4 (bluewifi=6): copy engines, HTC, WMI, passive scan

After WLAN_MODE mission (0168), bring up the WCN3990's host interface and
scan, polled from the watch thread. Ported from ios-topaz (MakrSas/
ios-topaz, APSL 2.0) xnu/patches/0123-topaz-wlan-scan.patch, itself a
port of ath10k snoc/ce/htc/wmi-tlv; ios-flame runs the same steps on the
Pixel 4. For SDM845:
- apps SMMU 0x15000000, WLAN stream 0x40 mask 0x1: ABL's entries for the
  stream are logged; a bypass entry (or bypass for unmatched streams) is
  kept, else the stream gets an identity context bank, before the WLAN
  block is powered;
- copy engines at 0x18800000+0x240000, shadow write indices at +0x32000;
- host memory from a 16 MiB pool at 0xe0000000 (free gap above the GPU
  pool, below XNU), write-combined.
HTC READY, HTT and WMI connects, SETUP_COMPLETE_EX, WMI SERVICE_READY ->
INIT -> READY, the HTT host rx ring (VERSION_REQ/CONF, frag desc bank,
RX_RING_CFG, AGGR_CFG; from ios-flame phone/wifi/radio.c, MIT: without it
no frame reaches the firmware's rx path), then a passive scan (nothing
transmitted); networks are logged once each, BSSIDs masked. A summary at
the end of the watch (bluewifi_watch).

Before the scan: the firmware's MAC over WLFW (0x33, a locally
administered address), PDEV_SET_REGDOMAIN (bluewifi_rd/_ctl), the
channel list with DFS flags on radar channels.

The scan covers the 13 2.4 GHz channels by default (bluewifi_nch=N; 37
adds 5 GHz UNII-1/2/2e/3): a scan that names any 5 GHz channel is
accepted but never starts. Tried without effect: the DFS and VHT flags,
regdomain 0x3a (FCC3_FCCA), L25a at 3.312 V, hardware mode 0
(bluewifi_hwmode=0: PDEV_SET_HW_MODE, answered status 0). A channel list
holding 5 GHz entries is fine; 2.4 GHz scans with it.

Diagnostics: WMI ECHO 2 s and 12 s after the scan request; the
firmware's log (WLFW INI enablefwlog, on unless bluewifi_fwlog=0) as WMI
DIAG events, hex; SERVICE_READY_EXT in hex; bluewifi_scanmode bits (1:
no channel list, 2: no scan channels, 4: no regdomain), bluewifi_clr5
(flags cleared on 5 GHz entries), bluewifi_nscan (scan only the first N
listed channels).

L25a (WLAN chain 0) is now 3.312 V, as in sdm845-google-common.dtsi
(bluewifi_ch0mv).

